                kb_claude "$KB_PB

TASK: Lint the wiki. Write a full report to $outdir/report.md covering:
1) Broken [[wikilinks]] (target page does not exist).
2) Orphaned wiki pages (no inbound links from any other wiki page or from _INDEX.md).
3) raw/ files not referenced in _SOURCES.md (unprocessed).
4) Frontmatter inconsistencies (missing title, type, tags).
5) Daily-note pollution in concepts/ (files matching pattern YYYY-MM-DD.md should probably move to journal/ or be merged).
6) Stale absolute paths (any wiki/_SOURCES.md row pointing at /Users/<other>/* is stale).
7) Top 5 highest-value new wiki pages to write next, given current raw/ contents.
End the report with a one-line summary."
                ;;
            query)
                q="$*"
                [[ -z "$q" ]] && die "Usage: qkz kb query \"your question\""
                cd "$KB_ROOT"
                rdate=$(date +%Y-%m-%d)
                slug=$(echo "$q" | tr '[:upper:] ' '[:lower:]-' | tr -dc 'a-z0-9-' | cut -c1-40)
                outdir="outputs/${rdate}_${slug}"
                mkdir -p "$outdir"
                kb_claude "$KB_PB

TASK: Answer this question USING THE WIKI.
Question: $q

Method (Karpathy navigation, no RAG):
1) Read wiki/_INDEX.md to find the relevant entry points.
2) Follow [[wikilinks]] to read the connected pages. Do not search blindly.
3) If a page you need does not exist but the raw/ has the source, note it as a follow-up.
4) Write $outdir/answer.md — the answer, with [[wikilinks]] inline as citations.
5) Write $outdir/slides.md — Marp deck (start with: \`---\nmarp: true\n---\`).
6) End answer.md with: '## Follow-ups' (5 questions) and '## File back into wiki' (changes to merge)."
                ;;
            ingest)
                exec python3 "$KB_ROOT/tools/ingest.py" "$@"
                ;;
            search)
                exec python3 "$KB_ROOT/tools/search.py" "$@"
